    "We'll ask iOS for permission next. You can change this any time in the Settings app." : {},
    "Welcome to LoopFollow" : {},
    "What is sent" : {},
    "What stays on your device" : {},
    "What's sent" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "When enabled, LoopFollow maintains a live connection to your Nightscout server using WebSocket while the app is in the foreground. Data updates (new glucose readings, treatments, device status) arrive within seconds instead of waiting for the next polling cycle.\n\nThe WebSocket disconnects when LoopFollow moves to the background and reconnects when you return to the app. Polling continues to handle updates while the app is in the background.\n\nIn the foreground, polling continues at a reduced frequency as a safety net. If the WebSocket connection drops, normal polling resumes immediately." : {},
    "Yes, send anonymous stats" : {},
    "You can change this any time in Settings → General → Diagnostics." : {},
    "You can choose to share anonymous information with the developers to help improve LoopFollow — such as app and iOS version, device type, which app you're following, and a few settings. Your health data, credentials, time zone, and logs remain on your device." : {},
    "You can choose to share anonymous information with the developers to help improve LoopFollow—such as app and iOS version, device type, which app you're following, and a few settings. Your health data, credentials, time zone, and logs remain on your device." : {},
    "You're all set" : {},
    "You're ready to go. Adjust everything later from the Menu — and when you have a moment, these are worth a look:" : {},
    "Your API secret is used once to create a read-only access token and is never stored." : {},
    "eHbA1c" : {},
    "eHbA1c — an A1c estimate from your average glucose. GMI — Glucose Management Indicator, another A1c estimate from average glucose. % and mmol/mol (IFCC) are two scales for the result." : {},
    "g" : {
      "comment" : "The short unit display string for grams"
    },
    "mg/dL" : {
      "comment" : "The short unit display string for milligrams of glucose per decilter"
    },
    "minutes" : {},
    "mmol/L" : {
      "comment" : "The short unit display string for millimoles of glucose per liter"
    },
    "mmol/mol" : {},
    "“Default Snooze” controls the default value for how long the alert stays quiet after you press Snooze. \"A snooze duration of 0 means the alarm is acknowledged (silenced), and will alert again next time the condition applies, without time limitation. \" Toggle “Snoozed” to mute this alarm right now." : {},
    "“Snooze All” disables every alarm. “Mute All” silences phone sounds but still vibrates and shows iOS notifications." : {},
